<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hamgyong Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hamgyong was one of the eight provinces of Joseon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, on the north-east coast of the peninsula bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a>. Mountainous and long a frontier against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a>, it was split in 1896 into North and South Hamgyong, which are now provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-korea">North Korea</a>. In ancient times its coast was home to the Okjeo and Dongye peoples.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hamgyong-province.jpg" alt="Hamgyong Province" width="320" height="520" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 고려 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hamgyong_Province_of_Late_Joseon_Dynasty.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
